I've queued the flock work to land again: a5e7f075 (flock) and 2b7329b4 (STATE.md), on main b35f308b. This time I didn't run a full build job (`--build`) first.

**Why it kept coming back:** #262 has been queued ahead of this issue since 11-19. It edits the same `just gates` line (it adds `uni-config`), so every batch that held both was sent back on a `justfile` conflict, even though main never moved.

**What changed:**
- `flock` is no longer on the `just gates` line. Its recipes (`just flock` and its go, java and rust legs) are still there.
- The notes in STATE.md, cross-test/TESTS.md and docs/DEVELOPMENT.md now say flock is not yet in `just gates`.
- PROPOSALS.md has a new entry to add `flock` back to that line once #262 is out of the way.
- I checked with `git merge-tree` that `justfile` now merges cleanly with #262's branch. PROPOSALS.md still conflicts, but the manager merges that file itself. STATE.md also still conflicts; if it does in the land, the manager drops our STATE.md commit and the next run redoes it.

**What I checked:**
- Locally, `just generate`, `go vet ./pkg/...` and `go test ./scripts/ ./pkg/...` pass.
- The flock code is the same as in the tree that passed the full gates with flock included (build pipeline 3096760179). Taking a gate off the line can't make the others fail; the land's own build runs the full gates again.

**Left for the next run**, once the manager gives its verdict:
- **If it merges:** a small follow-up commit that puts `flock` back on the gates line before `tacplus-script`, rebased on #262 once that merges. Then the outcome comment and closing #206.
- **If it's sent back:** fix it and land again.
